/**
 * @mainpage rude API Reference
 *
 * `rude` is a C++23 Reliable UDP Engine built on Boost.Asio. It provides
 * packet encoding, reliable and unreliable channel primitives, congestion
 * control policies, socket statistics, and a session abstraction.
 *
 * The stable API is centered on a small set of composable components:
 *
 * - @ref rude::DefaultCodec encodes and decodes the wire packet format.
 * - @ref rude::ReliableOrderedChannel delivers reliable data in sequence.
 * - @ref rude::ReliableUnorderedChannel delivers reliable data once without
 *   enforcing receive order.
 * - @ref rude::UnreliableChannel delivers only the newest sequenced data.
 * - @ref rude::ChannelConfig describes session channel profiles.
 * - @ref rude::SessionConfig describes session-level transport settings.
 *
 * Typical channel configuration:
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * auto ordered = rude::ChannelConfig::reliableOrdered(0);
 * ordered.sendWindow_ = 128;
 *
 * auto updates = rude::ChannelConfig::unreliableSequenced(1);
 *
 * rude::SessionConfig session;
 * session.maxChannels_ = 2;
 * @endcode
 *
 * Include @c rude/rude.hpp for the stable component/session surface, or include
 * narrower headers when build time matters.
 */
